    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that rejects creating an owner whose lower-cased email is already used by any other owner, responding with **409 Conflict**.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`DuplicateOwnerEmailException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending email, mirroring the existing `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, the normalized (lower-cased) email is now computed before saving and passed to a new `rejectDuplicateEmail(...)` guard. That method ignores a `null` email (email is optional), and compares case-insensitively against all existing owners' emails (skipping owners with no email), throwing the exception on a match.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DuplicateOwnerEmailException` that returns a 409 `ProblemDetail` with an `errors: [\"email\"]` property, consistent with the existing duplicate-telephone/household handlers.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` passes and `BUILD SUCCESS` is reported.",
