        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a faithful, additive replica of the existing duplicate-rejection patterns already established in this codebase, and everything lands in the right unit:\n\n- `DuplicateOwnerEmailException` mirrors `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` precisely (transient field, message-in-super, getter) \u2014 the natural home for a new conflict type.\n- The `ExceptionControllerAdvice` handler mirrors `handleDuplicateOwnerTelephoneException`, reuses the shared `detailBuild` helper and the `errors` property convention, and adds a parallel `ERROR_DUPLICATE_EMAIL` constant alongside the sibling constants.\n- `rejectDuplicateEmail` sits right next to `rejectDuplicateTelephone`/`rejectDuplicateHousehold` and follows the same `reject*` naming and stream-based structure; it is wired into `createOwner` in the same normalize\u2192reject\u2192set sequence already used for telephone. The null-guard is a reasonable, well-documented deviation justified by email being optional (unlike telephone).\n\nNo logic is duplicated (the shared `findAllOwners()` scan matches the existing idiom), no class is becoming a catch-all, and a maintainer here would find the shape immediately familiar."
